[{"id":"VRCE-2-14-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":1,"english":"Sumantra, well versed in legends, after passing by the gateways crowded with people, reached the solitary apartment (of Rāma).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ceb1be59fec19444df8bb4189337ccc6a1adefb7f8f1293c05b2bf3b0ca93c9","compact":"05a2a0a58b2908a3aeb828c5e603bd25b0734d217dd48a2a60060b622d6a425a","nasal":"3693f47e7ba8b3378d8bf4a73fff4d801b01f388d449b0ba6882d041a5e74393"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":2,"english":"Having youthful warders, carrying dares and bows, wearing ear-rings, cautious, attentive and devoted and saw (seated at the gate) several old men commanding female warders, mindful of duty, wearing red cloths and excellent ornaments, and having rattans in their hands.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e22f6775a7243025e028d23e5c4a0f9337c2cc5a12c6d57c98d4efb3c8e8b435","compact":"5756833f074ea1807eb4fc0358dfcbf3a95164b11463a76a90fdfd624a814651","nasal":"2b705e2bf991ff3471423d662805fc143e419cf2822c3a340eef3a42f5d854c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":3,"english":"Having youthful warders, carrying dares and bows, wearing ear-rings, cautious, attentive and devoted and saw (seated at the gate) several old men commanding female warders, mindful of duty, wearing red cloths and excellent ornaments, and having rattans in their hands.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"37fd70ffdd8fe155d2798480ea1f4cfa9196519b82be9ed8c1296ac198cdc9fb","compact":"577a610e02a7d430f226060ba24d71dcde86f98a55e4b287f97f5309f207d28a","nasal":"94522f1aeb8536617bf03ca49ef28e94a42edadaa99a8a2c9c1c6875dfd3f649"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":4,"english":"They all seeing Sumantra, ever wishing good to Rāma, approach, rose suddenly up from their seats with due respect. The humble minded charioteer then said to them, Go and speedily communicate to Rāma that Sumantra is waiting at the gate. At this the warders, desirous of doing good to their master, nearing Rāma, speedily communicated these words to him who was in the company of his wife.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-3","DUTT-2-16-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b3466d60728f0dc8584d00b69a8f87dca4748b934c992fe2cf44eed03646a92","compact":"6a37196f2fbb1008d9a82323917bc95b886d0010f49919fe7f718e017fb52fea","nasal":"185356274a739090bc8b8dc84bad06bdf96ad29c60ba22ee39ff049232b92cc8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":5,"english":"Rāma hearing of the arrival of his father's charioteer, ordered him to enter into the apartment, having his father's pleasure in view.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33ec9ed84de159042f12472ccff64588b57e4c28db2a08b84e1a744f444e8616","compact":"05daabdb693cf8a6a504e87e141026e7645e26f8de100a9240478d5c22da773f","nasal":"d4c81402d2225aadc273355bba33b5daa9ecdfa19ef74c4c7e240e7a428a0208"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":6,"english":"He (on entering) saw Rāma resembling Vaiśravaņa, will adorned and seated on a rolled sofa, with a beautiful coverlet on.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4a0547532e296f754796023e86956be6eb275ddc06e332b43cc86232d191e8e9","compact":"855c581806f38ded293fc6c811e3ed3e4986b253627fb60c8a3ee0a281724f30","nasal":"fde76d659584a93a7883a5cae25cba6d29a6ea73456b6eed0ae3bb71ec4c3ca8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":7,"english":"Having his body sprinkled with holy and fragrant sandal of the best kind, red as the blood of a hog; and having by him Sītā with a chowry in her hand, like moon himself in the company of citra.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c0c2c554038ed5807f648d1de7c56ee3dbb77b46e7d6121b86bd12925e93e0d9","compact":"a59fc741c7ea6f20688b72bdac39e092874304125a517a2aec27dc33975df2f9","nasal":"378f47737d59ddb9ad0d575334c20d43c046e5c808d291c348a06754aca115ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":8,"english":"Having his body sprinkled with holy and fragrant sandal of the best kind, red as the blood of a hog; and having by him Sītā with a chowry in her hand, like moon himself in the company of citra.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c4aef614335c469235ff3867458432d43c09d0eadeada6c8ec561c8a87c08143","compact":"550c1773061dbe61b5e507cea76d692093ab19a7794221c2614955fd7ab784ab","nasal":"550c1773061dbe61b5e507cea76d692093ab19a7794221c2614955fd7ab784ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":9,"english":"Whereupon Sumantra, acquainted with decorum, humbly saluted him (Rāma), the conferrer of great boons, and resplendent like the mid-day sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b981808dff6e9453bdf4afef47e14199877d887eb011ba2306a121353fd6a11c","compact":"c8254ec1a0bbb850afbedbb1b97c9f955abf25d5ae1cee5c9138f8f37fcc7372","nasal":"564def29f9250636e2002c1dd0ad4a68c59bf3798a12933696b3c66acf99817d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":10,"english":"And he well honoured by the king, seeing the king's son seated on the sleeping sofa with a delighted countenance, spoke these words to him with clasped hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"684bebacd7222bb9c06a96780998d3dc95c036c227a97d32e36e6ed5fdeda990","compact":"02b95bc2a5d294adcf761c9d0177b3e4a0d61b788feb2aac7aa9dff9fae084db","nasal":"2483064e34e4c93535dd12d726146384b848c6f84b8eb1480c09dbf5085cdc22"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":11,"english":"Oh, Rāma, great son of Kausalyā, your father and the queen Kaikeyi want to see you; so it behove you to go there without delay.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.582,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8cb4776d6dba0fff0b3ea84c23a8f6585c90fa9136be92cfd371f39b1fa71e1c","compact":"8a9e9f49368e08418a83456c70e0cfa3af7175cddb114bc47592c0348dace1a0","nasal":"8a9e9f49368e08418a83456c70e0cfa3af7175cddb114bc47592c0348dace1a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":12,"english":"Being pleased with these words the mighty hero of great effulgence, honoured his father's behest and spoke to Sītā thus.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f410cf9f3b5c88752ee6c898d623c6374e118b86f802b916f13ab56969932957","compact":"c4f0bccf6e0ace81d664d2ef4640083bc986a7f4b3f9060750cca98d2c5efdb5","nasal":"c4f0bccf6e0ace81d664d2ef4640083bc986a7f4b3f9060750cca98d2c5efdb5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":13,"english":"Oh, darling, doubt there is none that my father, going to Kaikeyi. is parleying with her regarding my installation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dcd9c2a355e9d4632557fb37cd6a1d6e7d68b1ff4423aa768769f2562eda85c8","compact":"6845623aa51b43a02b8be92915277239d8ef72d50a534f81eb9428c9cc697c1d","nasal":"8e1fa2ae1697e4bbced4e3d4769c7e3c969ac8fb3d29fea4c627e603484f013c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":14,"english":"Conceiving the king's intention that clever lady, of dark eyes and desirous of doing good to the king, that mother, the daughter of the king of Kekaya, pleased and intent upon king's welfare as will as upon that of mine, is hastening the monarch for my installation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.694,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8cdce718adecfdb0570fd8c7066f93183d017d461aba7ac72205516035ea94ad","compact":"87085b856fadc1580a852f12b0f1468e33a1d355195ce3f448f730764cac66a1","nasal":"87085b856fadc1580a852f12b0f1468e33a1d355195ce3f448f730764cac66a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":15,"english":"Worthy of the meeting at the inner apartment, the messenger has come, and I doubt not that the monarch shall install me to-day as the heirapparent of his throne.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c405e76f49686277bdbfb6ff0f1b581070a0fca1199194d98a571a1c68b3313","compact":"8d23531d2814b0e786a73345d5d9283a99fec6417f239a7141eac78508043429","nasal":"8d23531d2814b0e786a73345d5d9283a99fec6417f239a7141eac78508043429"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":16,"english":"Therefore I shall speedily go hence and see my father. Do you remain and enjoy here the company of your friends.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea29b0e044f3e9905de2801a35cc51e7dbb7dad89ea24e59a7cc0302d8129f44","compact":"1ca37cd43ae56ee47a389af468fd5f49faea13bd97ab47b79538fb7c0f8fec41","nasal":"42b8359abdf66e5f53dab580dbc81cdbdd70260f5ed8b11d716eb1016a2a8083"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":17,"english":"Regarded by her husband, Sītā of dark eyes and intent upon her husband's welfare, followed him to the entrance and said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce52a8a3f6211ad91dd1b6b96d7d61c296bfa815e679746e3b61892093ba314a","compact":"41c6e6b42a65428e0cfded6f57f593ea005aba1fb2ef902be8ec105df10f2464","nasal":"4df0a80cf9f34278459365702f3f681018c3c485f677e00c4453f15a2734f69c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":18,"english":"And met all his friends assembled at the middle apartment. Then that great son of the king, casting a glance upon them all who were present there to see him and pleasing them with sweet words ascended, like to the thousand-eyed Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0abf72503daed2da9f9121d772e921ede26a9907c963c259c6c9c4a20a30671","compact":"31df6ee4514da2110b29b48f936c58f54b2a500eb83e5425251373be3c52b6a2","nasal":"2218d41352888d6dc1de35f03711863d960f8ee6bcd9c17c88c3d7dcb302a98a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":19,"english":"It had two excellent horses tied to it like to two young elephants, and was of quick motion, resembling that of Indra's chariot carried by his horses.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.426,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"928f294b2ed4a144ebc9cd0630586f1dff7f25c3341c60c9029bb6479453c10d","compact":"d2df1e75cba1cf0fea09e826f28a22247d1e3f700a1a34c6f7fcb67693bc63ef","nasal":"4f01ace9f15278e108c5abc86784c383a46f6da191e93bd890b9267a279517b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":20,"english":"It had two excellent horses tied to it like to two young elephants, and was of quick motion, resembling that of Indra's chariot carried by his horses. Ascending the car, Raghava, of great effulgence, went speedily on, making (the space) resounded like to the muttering cloud on the sky. He issued out of his abode like the beautiful moon passing through a huge cloud.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.446,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-24","DUTT-2-16-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d299fc6cd87698d995c7659abc6c2472fb4f00e30edf307e1c431c9985ed9b2","compact":"874bd8e1320fb40fd5e3a984f7935ad436e755716dfab4dedf5ab786122c7750","nasal":"948a918ad10b156e7819668a9e9c7bff04dbb8ad872244f3407e1e657660696b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-14-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":14,"verse":21,"english":"Ascending the car, Raghava, of great effulgence, went speedily on, making (the space) resounded like to the muttering cloud on the sky. He issued out of his abode like the beautiful moon passing through a huge cloud. Lakşmaņa, the younger brother of Rāghava, standing behind him on the car with a splendid Chowry in his hand, began to guard his body.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.415,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-16-25","DUTT-2-16-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2014021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f8fd029713277003c391c215b4f09c5b3d48ee0dfb20ac